                "annotations": [],
                "text": "An analysis of the training examples reveals the transformation rule:\n\n1. Locate the 3x3 pattern of non-zero numbers in the input grid.\n2. Form a 3x3 binary mask indicating where the pattern contains non-zero values (1 where non-zero, 0 where zero).\n3. Tile the 3x3 pattern across the 9x9 output grid according to this mask: for each cell `(r, c)` of the 3x3 mask that is 1, copy the 3x3 pattern into the corresponding 3x3 block `(r, c)` of the output grid. Leave the remaining blocks filled with 0. (This is equivalent to the Kronecker product of the pattern's binary mask with the pattern itself).\n\nPlease provide the test input grid to solve.",
